---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const roadmap = [
  {
    number: "01",
    title: "Design your first agent",
    body: "Outcome, reasoning, tools, evidence, human control, evaluation.",
    status: "Available now",
    href: "/coach/",
  },
  {
    number: "02",
    title: "Make the agent reliable",
    body: "What happens when a run takes hours, a tool half succeeds, or the process restarts in the middle.",
    status: "Next",
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "State and memory",
    body: "What has to survive a restart, and what should be allowed to be forgotten.",
    status: "Planned",
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "Tools and authorization",
    body: "Who the agent is acting as, and what it is allowed to do on their behalf.",
    status: "Planned",
  },
  {
    number: "05",
    title: "Human control",
    body: "Approval, escalation, and the difference between oversight and a rubber stamp.",
    status: "Planned",
  },
  {
    number: "06",
    title: "Evaluation and verification",
    body: "Proving the system did the job, not that the model sounded right.",
    status: "Planned",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Coming next | Agent System Design Coach"
  description="The lesson roadmap for the Agent System Design Coach, and where to go in the meantime."
  pageSlug="coach"
>
  <div class="next shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">AGENT SYSTEM DESIGN COACH</p>
    <h1>Coming next</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Lesson 01 covers the decisions that make an agent useful when everything
      goes right. The rest of the series covers what happens when it does not.
      Lesson 02 is being written.
    </p>

    <ol class="roadmap">
      {
        roadmap.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <span class="roadmap__num">{item.number}</span>
            <div>
              <h2>
                {item.href ? <a href={item.href}>{item.title}</a> : item.title}
              </h2>
              <p>{item.body}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="roadmap__status">{item.status}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <div class="onward">
      <h2>In the meantime</h2>
      <p>
        The full treatment of everything above is already written up as course
        material, and it goes considerably deeper than a 10 minute lesson.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/learn/courses/agentic-system-design/"
            >Course 002: Agentic AI System Design</a
          >, seventeen modules from "should this be an agent" through to a
          capstone.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/learn/courses/long-running-agents/"
            >Course 001: Engineering Long-Running AI Agents</a
          >, which is lesson 02's subject in full, with fourteen failure labs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/fde-gym/">FDE Gym</a>, if you would rather be assessed than
          taught.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .next {
    max-width: 46rem;
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .roadmap {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .roadmap li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
  }

  .roadmap__num {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .roadmap h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .roadmap p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .roadmap__status {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .onward {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
  }

  .onward h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .onward p,
  .onward li {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .onward ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .onward li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .roadmap li {
      grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .roadmap__status {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
